  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_036: scvi_n200 + vit_l + avgpool + concat, 0.715 acc) establishes a strong baseline, but the RNA encoder axis remains critically under-explored: we have only tested pca_n2000 and scvi_n200, with zero evidence on scgpt. Config_048 (scgpt + vit_l + avgpool + concat, multiprofile) is a direct, single-variable comparison against config_036, isolating the effect of the RNA encoder in the most favorable multimodal setting. If scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, it opens a new promising direction; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 as the superior encoder and lets us focus remaining budget on aggregation/fusion refinements. Under a limited budget, resolving this high-uncertainty design axis is more informative than testing a second-order change (e.g., transformer aggregation, which prior RNA-only evidence suggests is inferior to avgpool)."
}

